# rule.always.spend-own-levers-before-escalation

a halt is a diagnosis to make, not a message to relay. the guard never says who owns each lever: sort by owner, spend yours first.

| lever | owner |
|---|---|
| `rhx route.stone.set --as absorbed --that <reviewer>` | driver |
| edit `$route/<stone>.guard` (`--paths-wout`/`--paths-with`, `--conversation`, `level`) | driver, once the mutate grant stands |
| diagnosed reviewer malfunction | driver |
| `rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N --stone <stone>` | driver, ONLY with a warrant |
| `rhx route.mutate grant allow` · `--as approved` · `--as overruled` · commit quota · `absent` credential · release auth | human |

no `rhx` command edits a guard; a hook seals it. `rhx route.mutate grant get` first: granted → edit; not → ask the human once per route. a hand-run `rhx review` is no lever (`rule.forbid.hand-run-reviews`). malfunction, self-review, and judge halts print remedies with no owner column: you sort.

## budget: refused by default

> inside the meter, taste counts. past the meter, only harm does.

all three owed: a **live urgent concession** · a **target reviewer run dry** · a `--stone` for **one** stone.

```sh
rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as conceded --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --severity urgent
rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N --peer <reviewer> --stone <s>
```

`urgent` = security · safety · monetary · reputation · behavioral, harm nameable; else `better` earns no round (`rule.always.concede-with-a-severity`). a bare `--add N` lands on the latest level only; pass `--level` or `--peer` for a lower one. `exhausted` with closed blockers: real harm → grade `urgent`; taste → the fix is the remedy.

test: **"is there a command i could run right now that would move this stone?"** yes → run it · no → surface the exact command the human must run.
